    "reasoning": "All 16 selected answers agree with their own captured worked solutions. q-79545: use denominator a to obtain (3a+2)/a, with a≠0. q-65242: factor sin³x and apply sin²x+cos²x=1. q-119387: the denominator simplifies to sin³θ, giving cotθ wherever the original expression is defined. q-141999: consecutive asymptotes at 0 and π/2 give B=2; the point (π/4,1) gives D=1, so B+2D=4. q-143672: the captured solution states a π/2 left shift, so 2C=π/2 and C=π/4; the supplied raster alone has no readable coordinate scale. For the parametric questions, differentiate dy/dx with respect to t and divide by dx/dt: q-50448 gives e^(-4t)(4t+1)/t³; q-54152 gives -2t⁵/3; q-78950 gives -sec³(2t); q-50242 gives -e^(2-5t)/6; q-78954 gives 14/t³, hence 7/4 at t=2; q-50018 gives -csc³(2t)/4, hence -2 at t=π/12. Hyperbola centers follow from the squared shifts: q-116103 (-6,-4), q-16381 (-6,7), q-78871 (5,-1), and q-78379 (2,3). q-11440: entrywise matrix addition gives rows (6,6) and (1,3). No submitted grades are supplied; every MA answer below is established by its own worked solution.",
